    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.tabline\n\n### Description\n\nIt would be incredibly useful if `mini.tabline` could display diagnostics and git diff indicators directly on each tab. This enhancement would help users quickly identify which tabs have errors, warnings, or modified content, without switching back and forth between buffers.\r\n\r\n## Proposed Features\r\n\r\n\t1.\tDiagnostics Indicator: Display error, warning, and hint counts (or icons) on each tab that correspond to the current diagnostics in the buffer.\r\n\t2.\tDiff Indicator: Show git status (modified, added, deleted) as part of the tab label.\r\n\r\n## Use Cases\r\n\r\n\t•\tEasily identify which buffers need attention (e.g., those containing errors or warnings) while navigating between multiple buffers/tabs.\r\n\t•\tQuickly spot modified files in a git repository, helping with version control workflows.\r\n\r\n## Possible Configurations\r\n\r\n\t•\tAllow users to configure which indicators to show (e.g., only errors, or all diagnostics).\r\n\t•\tCustomize the symbols/icons used for diagnostics and git diff.\r\n\t•\tOption to toggle the feature on/off via settings.\r\n\r\n## Benefits\r\n\r\n\t•\tStreamlines development workflows by providing immediate feedback on file statuses.\r\n\t•\tHelps users manage multiple buffers more efficiently by showing essential information at a glance.\r\n\r\n## References\r\n\r\n\t•\tOther plugins like `bufferline.nvim` have similar functionality, which could serve as inspiration for implementing this in `mini.tabline`.",
